<title>UK: UK's Major says EMU very unlikely to start in 1999.</title>
<headline>UK's Major says EMU very unlikely to start in 1999.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>British Prime Minister John Major said it was very unlikely but not impossible that European economic and monetary union would start on schedule in 1999.</p>
<p>&quot;We have concluded...that it is very unlikely, though not impossible, for the single currency itself to proceed safely on January 1, 1999,&quot; he told the House of Commons.</p>
<p>&quot;Not just Britain's participation -- the single currency itself...But if it did proceed without reliable convergence, we would not of course be part of it.&quot;</p>
<p>-- Richard Murphy, London Newsroom 44 171 542 2774</p>
</text>
